WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870
Lagos.

2
00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.690
Otodo-Gbame was a waterfront
community on the lagoon.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.510
By Amnesty International's estimate, over
30,000 of its residents were forcibly

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.670
evicted, in three
operations in 2016 and 2017.

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.070
London, 1974.

6
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.710
The Heygate estate is
completed in Southwark,

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.530
originally home to about 3,000 people.

8
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.930
By July 2014, it had been demolished.

9
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.410
Two neighbourhoods, two continents.

10
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.290
So who decides what
replaces a neighbourhood?

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.270
The residents?

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.130
The courts?

13
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.370
The market?

14
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.170
In this mission, you'll
compare the two cases:

15
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.350
their process, their scale, and
the evidence behind each account.

16
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.990
Then you'll weigh the responses, from
London's resident ballots to Barcelona's

17
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.010
Superblocks.

18
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.490
Your mission: decide who really
decides what replaces a neighbourhood.
